# WEFT: hold EDIT on WEFT PATCH and turn KNOB 1 (BLOCK): the block moves a place a detent, the others shift along,
# and everything that names it follows: cords, its settings' values, a matrix row and a step lock on them.
# PING SWITCH: 1 TICK, 2 RING (A 1; settings 3-4 = 11, 25), 3 RING (A 1, B 9; settings 5-6 = 13, 35), 6 SW 4>1 (A 2)
wait 300
kind 1 6
wpreset 1 17
setmat 1 1 3
setlock 1 1 4
tap EDIT
wait 50
turn SELECT 2
wait 100
expect page WEFT PATCH
turn K1 1
wait 100
press EDIT
wait 100
shot weft_move_held.png
turn K1 1
wait 100
shot weft_move.png
release EDIT
wait 200
expect page WEFT PATCH
expect wtype 1 3 25
expect wsrc 1 3 1
expect wsrcb 1 3 0
expect wsrcb 1 2 9
expect wsrc 1 6 3
expect wsetting 1 5 11
expect wsetting 1 6 25
expect wsetting 1 3 13
expect wsetting 1 4 35
expect matset 1 5
expect lockset 1 1 6
# two more places, then three back: the patch as it was
press EDIT
turn K1 2
wait 100
turn K1 -3
wait 100
release EDIT
wait 200
expect wsrc 1 6 2
expect wsrc 1 2 1
expect wsrcb 1 3 9
expect wsetting 1 3 11
expect wsetting 1 5 13
expect matset 1 3
expect lockset 1 1 4
expect page WEFT PATCH
# EDIT tapped on its own still does what it did (here, in EDIT already: the next page)
tap EDIT
wait 100
expect page WEFT BLOCK
